    {
      "id": "h2-names",
      "title": "What's your name?",
      "kind": "LEARN",
      "introduces": ["ich", "du", "heissen", "name", "mein", "wie", "und", "ja", "nein"],
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "h2-e1",
          "type": "TEACH",
          "title": "Asking someone's name",
          "body": "The verb **heißen** means *to be called*. Germans use it to give their name:\n\n- **Wie heißt du?** What's your name? (literally *How are you called?*)\n- **Ich heiße Anna.** My name is Anna.\n\nYou can also say **Mein Name ist Anna.** It sounds a little more formal.",
          "examples": [
            { "text": "Wie heißt du?", "translation": "What's your name?" },
            { "text": "Ich heiße Anna.", "translation": "My name is Anna." },
            { "text": "Mein Name ist Tom.", "translation": "My name is Tom." }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "h2-e2",
          "type": "TEACH",
          "title": "The letter ß",
          "body": "**ß** (called *Eszett*) is simply a sharp **ss** sound. It appears after long vowels and after *ei, au, eu*: *heißen, Straße*.\n\nUse the **ß** key under the answer box. If you type *ss* instead, the app accepts it but reminds you.",
          "examples": [
            { "text": "heißen", "translation": "to be called" },
            { "text": "Straße", "translation": "street" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "h2-e3",
          "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
          "prompt": "Wie heißt du?",
          "promptLanguage": "TARGET",
          "options": ["What's your name?", "How are you?", "Where are you from?"],
          "optionsLanguage": "BASE",
          "answerIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "h2-e4",
          "type": "WORD_ORDER",
          "translation": "My name is Anna.",
          "answer": "Ich heiße Anna.",
          "distractors": ["heißt", "du"]
        },
        {
          "id": "h2-e5",
          "type": "WORD_ORDER",
          "translation": "What's your name?",
          "answer": "Wie heißt du?",
          "distractors": ["heiße", "ich"]
        },
        {
          "id": "h2-e6",
          "type": "TEACH",
          "title": "ich and du",
          "body": "- **ich** = I (only capitalised at the start of a sentence)\n- **du** = you, when talking to one friend, family member or child\n\nThe verb ending changes with the person:\n\n- ich heiß**e**\n- du heiß**t** (usually *-st*, but the stem already ends in ß)",
          "examples": [
            { "text": "ich heiße", "translation": "I am called" },
            { "text": "du heißt", "translation": "you are called" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "h2-e7",
          "type": "CLOZE",
          "before": "Ich",
          "after": "Lisa.",
          "accepted": ["heiße"],
          "translation": "My name is Lisa.",
          "hint": "heißen → ich …"
        },
        {
          "id": "h2-e8",
          "type": "CLOZE",
          "before": "Wie",
          "after": "du?",
          "accepted": ["heißt"],
          "translation": "What's your name?",
          "hint": "heißen → du …"
        },
        {
          "id": "h2-e9",
          "type": "MATCH_PAIRS",
          "pairs": [
            { "target": "ich", "base": "I" },
            { "target": "du", "base": "you (informal)" },
            { "target": "ja", "base": "yes" },
            { "target": "nein", "base": "no" },
            { "target": "und", "base": "and" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "h2-e10",
          "type": "TRANSLATE",
          "source": "My name is Tom.",
          "sourceLanguage": "BASE",
          "accepted": ["Ich heiße Tom.", "Mein Name ist Tom."]
        },
        {
          "id": "h2-e11",
          "type": "TRANSLATE",
          "source": "Ja, ich heiße Max.",
          "sourceLanguage": "TARGET",
          "accepted": ["Yes, my name is Max.", "Yes, I am called Max.", "Yes, I'm called Max.", "Yes, I'm Max.", "Yes, I am Max."]
        },
        {
          "id": "h2-e12",
          "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
          "prompt": "nein",
          "promptLanguage": "TARGET",
          "options": ["no", "nine", "yes"],
          "optionsLanguage": "BASE",
          "answerIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "h2-e13",
